000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.    SINQRSI.
000400 AUTHOR.        BARBARA WINTER.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN.  DECEMBER 12, 1986.
000600 DATE-COMPILED.
000700*REMARKS.       SUBROUTINE THAT SHOWS RECEIVING SLIP ITEM DATA.
000800*************************************************************
000900*************************************************************
001000*                      S I N Q R S I                        *
001100*                                                           *
001200*    THIS SUBROUTINE SHOWS ITEM INFORMATION FOR ALL ITEMS   *
001300*    ON A RECEIVING SLIP.  ITEMS MAY BE BROWSED FORWARD AND *
001400*    BACKWARD.  RECEIVING SLIPS MAY ALSO BE BROWSED         *
001500*    FORWARD AND BACKWARD FROM ANY POINT.  THIS MEANS THAT  *
001600*    ONE OF FOUR CHOICES CAN BE MADE WHEN BROWSING;         *
001700*            1.  PREVIOUS ITEMS ON CURRENT RECEIVER         *
001800*            2.  MORE ITEMS ON CURRENT RECEIVER             *
001900*            3.  PREVIOUS RECEIVING SLIP                    *
002000*            4.  NEXT RECEIVING SLIP                        *
002100*                                                           *
002200*    THE FREIGHT INQUIRY MAY BE SELECTED AT ANY TIME ALSO.  *
002300*    THE FREIGHT INQUIRY WILL PICK UP FROM THE CURRENT      *
002400*    RECEIVING SLIP BEING REVIEWED IN THIS PROGRAM.  THERE  *
002500*    IS ONE EXCEPTION TO THIS RULE.  IF, IN THE MAIN        *
002600*    PROGRAM, THE USER ENTERED A PO AND CHOSE TO GO         *
002700*    DIRECTLY TO THE FREIGHT INQUIRY FIRST, THEN THE USER   *
002800*    CHOSE TO EXECUTE THIS RECEIVING SLIP INQUIRY FROM THE  *
002900*    FREIGHT INQUIRY, THE FREIGHT INQUIRY WILL BE CONSIDERED*
003000*    THE "DRIVING" PROGRAM AND THIS PROGRAM WILL PICK UP    *
003100*    THE RECEIVING SLIP LAST REVIEWED ON THE FREIGHT        *
003200*    SCREEN, ALLOW THE USER TO BROWSE FORWARD AND BACKWARD, *
003300*    BUT THEN RETURN TO THE FREIGHT INQUIRY ON THE RECEIVER *
003400*    WHERE THE FREIGHT HAD LEFT OFF.                        *
003500*************************************************************
003600*    CALLING PROGRAMS:                                      *
003700*       1.  SRSINQS  -  MAIN SUBROUTINE FOR RS INQUIRY      *
003800*       2.  SINQFRT  -  FREIGHT INQUIRY                     *
003900*************************************************************
      *************************************************************
      *C               HISTORY OF CHANGES
      *C
      *C  11/22/93  JEFF BUNGO  REQ # 4502
      *C      MODIFIED LOGIC TO GO TO HISTORY DATABASE FOR THE
      *C      INQUIRY IF THE PASS-HISTORY-FLAG IS SET TO "Y".
      *C
      *C  06/07/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C      EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C      RECOMPILE TO PICK UP NEW FILE FORMATS.
      *C
      *C  08/29/00  JIM COFFMAN
      *C      REMOVED CHECKS IN PARAGRAPHS 110-NEW-RECIEVER
      *C      AND 112-CHAINHD-DRCVITEM FOR RECEIVER NUMBER
      *C      GREATER THAN 998 ASA DANVILLE HAD A 999 RECEIVER
      *C      NUMBER AND THEY COULD NOT VIEW THE DATA.
      *C
      *C  04/16/02  CA YODER     (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C      ADDED SUBFILE LOGIC TO DISPLAY RECEIVING SLIP
      *C      DESCRIPTION.  ALSO ADDED CALL TO "CCRQDESC"
      *C      TO SHOW MP8 COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENT INFORMATION.
      *C      NOTE:  THIS PROGRAM NOW USES THE SCREEN PROGRAM
      *C      ZINQRS INSTEAD OF ZCSISINQ.
      *C
      *C  06/04/2003 WR FONAGY
      *C      ADD LOGIC TO ONLY DISPLAY A MAXIMUM OF 25 LINES
      *C      OF DESCRIPTION.  UNION CITY HAD BLOWUP DUE TO
      *C      A RECEIVING SLIP THAT CONTAINED 26 LINES OF
      *C      DESCRIPTION.
      *C***********************************************************
